Is there something between an ER and a walk-in clinic? Like when you need to see a doctor today, but it's not life-threatening? Turns out there is! It's called an Urgent Care Centre. It's where you can go for broken bones, serious illnesses and infections. Plus, it helps relieve the strain at the emerg. 

@drshazmamithani of @thedoctalkpod is here to break down how they work and why Canada doesn't have more of them, yet. 

